00:23:04.830 --> 00:23:07.798
So the Doge is the highest
author authority in Venice

00:23:07.798 --> 00:23:09.930
between the 11th and the 14th century.

00:23:09.930 --> 00:23:12.970
And the selection of
the Doge was entrusted

00:23:12.970 --> 00:23:16.620
as Greif and Laitin summarized
in this passage here,

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:18.930
to a committee, which was itself,

00:23:18.930 --> 00:23:22.650
selected by a combination
of lot and delegation.

00:23:22.650 --> 00:23:27.650
And the process was famously
extraordinarily complicated,

00:23:27.810 --> 00:23:29.220
involving nine steps.

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:30.357
And so again, we see the lot,

00:23:30.357 --> 00:23:33.720
and this is perhaps a
point that is relevant also

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:36.240
for some of the questions
in the round table later.

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:39.060
The lot here is not just a
sort of like a unique system

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:42.659
of selection that is
presented as better or worse

00:23:42.659 --> 00:23:45.586
or for particular reasons,
depending on the particular sort

00:23:45.586 --> 00:23:48.508
of needs of the society,
but it is really part

00:23:48.508 --> 00:23:51.330
of a much more complex system

00:23:51.330 --> 00:23:55.590
of selection that is aimed
at a variety of outcomes,

00:23:55.590 --> 00:23:59.010
including some of the outcomes
that Allie has discussed.

00:23:59.010 --> 00:24:02.160
Particularly the sort of like attempt

00:24:02.160 --> 00:24:05.156
at eliminating elite
capture by, in this case,

00:24:05.156 --> 00:24:09.810
clans and social groups
within the polity of Venice.

00:24:09.810 --> 00:24:12.750
In Athens, the lot was
used much more broadly.

00:24:12.750 --> 00:24:17.250
In fact, the three of the
four main institutions

00:24:17.250 --> 00:24:20.100
included the use of the
lot one way or another.

00:24:20.100 --> 00:24:21.990
The third, the fourth being the assembly,

00:24:21.990 --> 00:24:24.493
that was where members were selected on

00:24:24.493 --> 00:24:26.340
a first come, first serve basis.

00:24:26.340 --> 00:24:30.179
But in looking at the other
three main institutions

00:24:30.179 --> 00:24:33.360
in the polity of Athens,
we see that again,

00:24:33.360 --> 00:24:36.990
like, the lot was used
abundantly and differentially.

00:24:36.990 --> 00:24:39.513
In the council that I will
talk about more in a second,

00:24:39.513 --> 00:24:44.310
it was used for the selection
of a representative sample

00:24:44.310 --> 00:24:46.620
of jurors in the courts.

00:24:46.620 --> 00:24:50.040
It was very interestingly,
again for dorks in the room,

00:24:50.040 --> 00:24:54.120
well known to be used on a
daily basis for the selection

00:24:54.120 --> 00:24:56.432
of jury panels in the law courts

00:24:56.432 --> 00:24:58.620
through the system known as Kleroterion.

00:24:58.620 --> 00:25:01.440
This is the part where
I sort of like flash you

00:25:01.440 --> 00:25:04.380
this like ancient system of randomization

00:25:04.380 --> 00:25:05.644
that the Athenians used.

00:25:05.644 --> 00:25:10.380
And in the council again, it was used in a

00:25:10.380 --> 00:25:14.520
slightly different way that
I will talk about in greater

00:25:14.520 --> 00:25:16.020
depth in a moment, sorry.

00:25:16.020 --> 00:25:18.630
And with the magistrates, it was also used

00:25:18.630 --> 00:25:22.320
for the selection of some
